Bone.; Os.
Bony.; Osseus.
Ossified.; Ossificatus.
See <Flesh>.

@AC 41. Man's proprium... appears bony... @149[2].

@148. "Bones" = those things which are lower, because having the least vitality.

@149. "Bones" in the Word = the proprium, in fact the proprium vivified by the Lord. Illustrated.

@--[end]. The Lord's proprium is signified by... "a Spirit hath not flesh and bones as ye see Me have."

@156. "Bone of bones" (Genesis 2:23) = the proprium of the outward man; "bone" = the proprium not so much vivified... @157.

@827[end]. They become at last as it were bony...

@2441[end]. To "spread out the bones" (Jeremiah 8:2) = the infernal things with such.

@2492[2]. With those who have been deceitful and hypocrites (the memory) appears as it were bony, and of ebony.

@2916[3]. The vivified "bones" (Ezekiel 37). @TCR 594.

@3812. "My bone and my flesh" (Genesis 29:14) = conjunction (as to truths and as to goods). Explained. "Bone" = the intellectual proprium... thus the proprium as to truth.

@--[3]. Hence "bones" in the Word = truth, and in the opposite sense, falsity. Fully illustrated.

@--[8]. Truth supports good as bones do the flesh. @9634[2].

@4630. A smell as of burnt horn or bone. @5573. @SE 3206. @3498.

@5552. On the correspondence of the bones. General article. @SE 920. @5141.

@5560. The Societies of Spirits to which the cartilages and bones correspond are very numerous. They are such as have very little spiritual life...

@5561. Other Spirits speak through those who relate to the bones, they themselves knowing little of what they say, but still they talk, placing all their delight in it. To such a state are those reduced who have led an evil life, and yet have some remains of good stored up in them...

@5562. They who emerge from vastations, and serve for such uses as the bones do, have no determinate thought... @SE 920.

@6359. When falsity... is confirmed by many things, a hardness appears like the hardness of bone.

@6380. The hard things with man, as the teeth, bones, cartilages, correspond to truths and goods of the lowest Natural.

@6389. "A bony donkey" (Genesis 49:14) = lowest service. "Bone" = what has little spiritual life in it. @AE 445[4].

@6592. "Ye shall cause my bones to go up from here" (Genesis 1:25) = that there shall be a representative of the Church... "Joseph's bones" = that which is the most external, or the ultimate of the Church, thus its representative... @8101.

@7748. (Correspondence of ossification.)

@8005. "Ye shall not break a bone in it" (Exodus 12:46) = that scientific truth shall be entire. "A bone" = the ultimate in which the interior things are terminated as in their base, that they may be supported in such a manner as to prevent spreading out. Such an ultimate in spiritual things is the Scientific... Scientifics are as the bones in man; if they are not entire, or in their own order, as when out of joint, or distorted, the form of the body is varied, and the actions according thereto.

@9163[4]. To "break the bones" (Exodus 12:46) = to destroy the truths from the Divine which are last in order, on which rest and by which are supported interior truths and goods, and which if destroyed cause the whole superstructure to fall. Ultimate truths are those of the letter of the Word... on which the interior truths rest... That bones = truths, References.

@9209[6]. "Bones" (Psalms 35:10) = scientific truths.

@9407[9]. "The bones which were ruddy" (Lamentations 4:7) = scientific truths which are ultimate, and serve the rest.

@9643[2]. Under <Base>, see this reference.

@9916. (The use of the bones below the neck.)

@10037[2]. "The bones of kings and princes drawn out of the graves" (Jeremiah 8:1) = truths profaned; "the bones of priests and prophets" = goods profaned.

@10105[4]. "The thigh, shoulder, and choice of the bones" (Ezekiel 24:4) = Divine truths from Divine good in successive order.

@10287[2]. After this tearing to pieces (profaners) scarcely appear as men, but as burnt bones...

@10429. Such (as are merely external) appear as it were bony without life as to the head and face...

@HH 354[2]. The interiors of those who have confirmed themselves against the Divine... are ossified.

@553[2]. With many of the infernals no face appears, but in place of it something hairy, or bony.

@DLW 304. Until (the fibres) become cartilages and bones.

@DP 227[5]. (Profaners) no longer appear as men, but as bones with some skin drawn over them.

@254[3]. (The heathen) constitute those things which are called the skins, membranes, cartilages, and bones.

@CL 263. In place of feet ankles of bone without flesh.

@512[2]. (Violators) appear as consisting of bones with only some skin drawn over.

@SE 3888. (Origin of the bones of the skull by the induration of the membranes.) @3913.

@3910. (On those who can only be amended so as to become scarcely self conscious, as the bones are, in which however there is some life.) @3912. @3944.

@5141. Those correspond to the bones who have studied various sciences and have made no use of them...

@5575. The celestial correspond to... the flesh, even to the tendinous parts, the cartilaginous and bony ones.

@AE 167[5]. "My bone was not hid from Thee when I was made in secret" (Psalms 139:15) = that no falsity which was made was hidden... "Bone" = truth in the ultimate of order, and in the opposite sense, falsity. References. @196[end].

@313[11]. "Bones" (Jeremiah 23:9) = ultimates.

@364[5]. "Bones" (Lamentations 4:7) = truths in their own ultimate, thus truths in the whole complex.

@418[3]. "Dry bones" (Ezekiel 37) = those in whom there is nothing of spiritual life. @419[3].

@513[19]. "Flesh and bones" (Luke 24:39) = man's ultimates.

@555[14]. "Bone" (Genesis 2:23) = truth before it is vivified, that is, conjoined with good, as is truth of the memory.

@619[15]. His "bones" (Luke 24) = the truths of the ultimate.

@659[3]. "A man's bone" (Numbers 19:16) = infernal falsity.

@--[14]. "The bones" (Ezekiel 37) = truths in the ultimate of order upon which spiritual truths are founded; but "dry bones" = falsities from evil.

@--[24]. "Bones" (Jeremiah 8:1) = falsities and evils.

@665[4]. The Church is compared to "dry bones" (Ezekiel 37), because they have no good of love and truth of doctrine. @666[3].

Book.; Liber.
Little Book.; Libellus.

@AC 469. "The book of the nativities" (Genesis 5:1) = an enumeration of those who were of the Most Ancient Church.

@1540[end]. All the books of the ancients were written (by representatives). Such is the book of Job; Solomon's Song is an imitation of them; such were the two books mentioned in Numbers 21:14, 27. @1756[2]. @2588[6]. @2686. @2762[2]. @3179[end]. @3482. @3942[2]. @DSS 20.

@2178[end]. Books not thus written were accounted as valueless, those within the Church as without holiness... Hence the books of the Word were thus written.

@3901[6]. The books of that time were almost all written by means of significatives.

@4280. That the knowledge of representatives was their wisdom is evident from the oldest books of the Gentiles. @4966. @5223. @9293[3]. @9407[4].

@4735[10]. "The book of the covenant" (Exodus 24:7) = the Divine truth which they then had.

@5620[13]. "The little book" (Revelation 10) = truth Divine.

@6752[4]. "The book of the law" (Deuteronomy 31:24) = the books of Moses... "The Law of Jehovah" (Psalms 1) = the books of Moses, for the prophetical books and the historical ones, except the books of Joshua and Judges did not yet exist.

@6811. (Spirits read man's memory like a book.)

@8379. Their houses are lined inside with bark...

@8620. To "write in a book" (Exodus 17:14) = for perpetual remembrance. Illustrated.

@9049[2]. The laws of order in the other life are not learned from books... but are written on hearts...

@9341[7]. That Jeremiah "bound a stone to the book" written by himself (Jeremiah 51:63) = that the prophetic Word was perishing through the like things.

@9386[2]. Man has as it were two books in which are written all his thoughts and acts; these books are his two memories. (See <Memory>.)

@9396. "He took the book of the covenant" (Exodus 24:7) = the Word in the letter, with which the Word in Heaven is conjoined. "Book" = the Word in the whole complex. Explained.

@10325. The books of the Word are all those which have an inward sense. Enumerated. @NJHD 266.

@10505. "Blot me out of thy book which Thou hast written" (Exodus 32:32) = that the internal of the Word, of the Church, and of worship will not perish... "Book" = what is in the internal... That "the book which Jehovah has written," called elsewhere "the book of life" = what is internal. Explained.

@HH 269. The Angels can recite in a few words the contents of any book.

@462. a. 3. Their very memorandum books... were opened and read before them, page by page.

@463[2]. I have seen books with writings in them as in the world which were taken from the memory of their authors, not a word being wanting...

@DP 213[end]. Write books... in favour of human prudence and nature, and put them into the hand of any Angel...

@AR 256. "A book written within and on the back" (Revelation 5:1) = the Word in every particular and every general.

@--[2]. As the Word is meant by "a book"... it is said to be "written in the book," to be "judged out of the book," to be "blotted out of the book," where the state of the eternal life of anyone is treated of. Illustrated.

@259. To "open the book and loose its seals" (Revelation 5:2) = to know the states of life of all in the Heavens and on earth, and also to judge everyone according to his state, for when the book is opened, an examination of their character takes place, and then the sentence is pronounced; as a judge does with and from a book of law. @295.

@335. "Heaven departed as a book rolled up" (Revelation 6:14) = separation from Heaven and conjunction with Hell... A book rolled up means a parchment rolled up, for their books were parchments, and comparison is made with a book, because "the book" = the Word. @AE 299[3]. @404[end].

@469. "He had in His hand a little book open" (Revelation 10:2) = the Word as to the doctrine therein that the Lord is the God of Heaven and earth, and that His Human is Divine. Explained. @472.

@481. To "take the little book" (Revelation 10:8) = to receive the doctrine concerning the Lord.

@867. "The books were opened, and another book was opened which is that of life" (Revelation 20:12) = that the interiors of the minds of them all were thrown open... "The books" = the interiors of the mind of those who are evil, and are judged to death, and "the book of life" those who are good and are judged to life. They are called "books" because on the interiors of the mind of everyone are inscribed all things which each has thought, intended, spoken, and done in the world from the will and thence the understanding.

@875[15]. (A book seen there which was the Divine Love and Wisdom.)

@944. "The prophecy of this book" = the doctrine of this book now opened by the Lord.

@CL 207[5]. Books in the Spiritual World. @380[3]. @SE 4711. @5561. @5602.

@TCR 335. (False lights seen, like open books; some flew upwards and perished; others fell and turned to dust.)

@814. This state (of the Germans is represented in the Spiritual World by a man who carries books under his arms, and who reads the answer to every question out of one of the books.)

@SE 385. (On the lot of bookworms.)

@5999. (On the study of books there.)

@AE 299. "A book written within and on the back" = the state of life of all in Heaven and earth, in general and particular. @303.

@306[end]. "A book" = all things which are with a man, Spirit, and Angel, or all their states of life as to love and faith; wherefore to "open the book" = to know these things; to "read the book" = to know them; and to "look into the book" = to investigate them.

@404. "As a book rolled up" = that it was closed.

@569[21]. "The book of the prophet" (Jeremiah 51:63) = the Word which was in the book, in general, the whole Word.

@LJPost 99. The Mohammedans have a book in which are some pages written by correspondences.

@LJPost 121. The Africans have had a book since ancient times which is written by correspondences. @SE 5809[end].

@5M 18. Heaps of half open books seen.

@5M 19. The tables and half open books were representatives of the intentions of the mind and thence of the deeds according to which they will be judged faithful and unfaithful.

Book of life.; Liber vitae.

@AC 2256[2]. (Everything) is inscribed in his book of life, that is, his two memories and his nature...

@2474. This is his book of life which is opened in the other life... @SE 2156.

@8620[2]. "Books" in these passages = the recollection of all things which they have done, for everyone takes with him into the other life the memory of all his acts, thus the book of his life. Illustrated.

@9841[3]. The interior or spiritual memory is the book of man's life. @DP 227.

@10505. Under <Book>, see this reference, and at @AR 867.

@--[3]. "They who are written in the book of life" = those who are in the life of truth and good, thus who, from love and faith, do the Divine commandments... Illustrated.

@HH 236[end]. The Angels know all things of another's life from some ideas of his thought, because thence they know his reigning love, in which are all things in their order. Man's book of life is nothing else.

@463. Man's "book of life" means that all things both done and thought are inscribed on the whole man, and appear as if read in a book when called forth from the memory, and as if seen in effigy when the spirit is viewed in the light of Heaven. Described.

@AR 588. "The book of life" (Revelation 13:8) = the Word of the Lord, and all doctrine concerning Him.

@735. "Whose names were written in the book of life from the foundation of the world" (Revelation 17:8) = who do not believe in the Lord, and are not in doctrine from the Word.

@874. "If anyone was not found written in the book of life" (Revelation 20:15) = those who have not lived according to the Lord's injunctions in the Word.

@925. "But they who are written in the Lamb's book of life" (Revelation 21:27) = that none are received into the New Church... but those who believe in the Lord and live according to His injunctions in the Word.

@958. To "take away their part out of the book of life" (Revelation 22:19) = that they cannot acquire any wisdom from the Word, or appropriate anything from it. "The book of life" = the Word, and also the Lord as to the Word. References. The reason is that the Lord is the Word... @TCR 107.

@SE 4430. (Opening of man's book of life there.) @4701, Example(s).

@AE 199. "I will not blot out his name out of the book of life" (Revelation 3:5) = that they will be in Heaven... "The book of life" = Heaven. Explained... "The book of life" is that with man which corresponds to Heaven with him. Explained, Illustrated.

Bookcase.; Librarium. @TCR 343. @692[3]. @694[5]. @797[2]. @--[end].

Bookworm. See <Book> at @SE 385.

Borders. See <Boundary>.

Border.; Confinium. @TCR 279.
See <Fringe>.

Border.; Limbus.

@AC 9492. "A border (of gold on the ark)" (Exodus 25:11) = termination from good lest they be approached and injured by evils. "A border" = termination. Explained. @10187.

@9496[2]. The "border" had reference to the circumference (in man) in which there is termination.

@9533. "Thou shalt make for (the table) a border of gold round about" (Exodus 25:24) = the termination of the sphere of good from the Lord's Divine good.

@9535. "Thou shalt make a border of gold of the closure round about" (Exodus 25:25) = the termination of the sphere of Divine good.

@9914. "A lip," or "border," round the upper opening of the robe (Exodus 28:32) = terminated and closed on every side.

@10835. (A border round the roof.)

@CL 29[2]. (The departed believed to be in limbo.)

@TCR 74. (The borders of their hats.)

@103. After death... man retains the Spiritual from the father, together with a certain limbus from the purest things of nature around it; but with those who come into Heaven this limbus is below and the Spiritual above, whereas with those who come into Hell this limbus is above and the Spiritual below. (See @DLW 257[5]. @DWis 8. 7.)

Bore.; Perforare.
See <Awl>.

@AC 5145. "Perforated upon my head" (Genesis 40:16) = without termination anywhere in the middle. "Perforated" means open from top to bottom, thus not closed.

Borer.; Terebra.
Boring.; Terebratio.

