@AC 986[2]. Man is born again through truths of faith. @HH 342. [Swedenborg footnote 1.]

@3701[3]. He ought to be born again as an infant.

@3860. Regeneration is called rebirth, but spiritual.

@5115[2]. The man who is being born again...

@5130[3]. The rebirth of the Sensual subject to the intellectual part, Treated of. @5122.

@10367[3]. In order to be delivered from Hell, man must be wholly born again by the Lord. It is this rebirth which is called regeneration. In order therefore that he may be born again he must first learn truths...

@HH 279. Regeneration is rebirth as to the spiritual man. Described.

Borrow.; Mutuum accipere.
See <Lend-Commodare>, also see <Ask-Petere>.

@AE 556[9]. "From him who would borrow of thee turn not thou away" (Matthew 5:42) = if he longs to be instructed, instruct him; for the evil long for this in order to pervert and deprive, but are not able.

Bosom.; Gremium.

@AC 1736[3]. To "carry in the bosom" (Isaiah 40:11) is predicated of His love or mercy.

@TCR 508[3]. A golden image in his bosom...

@582[2]. As one who warms a serpent in his bosom.

Bosom.; Sinus.
See <Breast>.

@AC 3305[7]. To be "in Abraham's bosom" (Luke 16:22) = in the Lord (from conjunction through love). @6960[3].

@4048[end]. Such are they who relate to the sinuses or greater blood-vessels of the brain; and they who resemble such relate to the longitudinal sinus between the two hemispheres of the brain, which is in a state of quiet however the brain on each side may be agitated. @7744[end]. @SE 3879.

@6960. "Convey thy hand into thy bosom" (Exodus 4:6) = the appropriation of truth... "Bosom" = love; for what belongs to the breast corresponds to love... And as the bosom corresponds to love, it also = the proprium, for that is proper to man which is of his love; therefore here, to "convey the hand into the bosom" = appropriation. Illustrated.

@--[2]. "Lying in the bosom" (Micah 7:5) = one who is conjoined through love. Hence a wife is called "the wife of her husband's bosom" (Deuteronomy 28:54 and 2 Samuel 12:8), and a husband is called "the husband of the wife's bosom" (Deuteronomy 28:56), and this because the one is the other's.

@--. "Bosom" (Psalms 35:13) = himself.

@--[3]. To "give into the bosom" (Luke 6:38) = to themselves as their Own. @--[end].

@--[4]. To "lean on the bosom" (John 13:23) = to be loved, and to be conjoined through love. @10087[2]. @--[end].

@--[5]. "Bosom" = that which actually belongs to man, and appropriation not through love, in the following. Illustrated.

@6997[7]. (The interior and the inmost bosom of the Word.)

@AE 821[6]. "Bosom" and "breast," in the Word = spiritual love, which is love in act; and the Lord's "bosom" and "breast" (John 13:23) = the Divine love itself; wherefore they are in the province of the breast in Heaven who are in spiritual love.

Botany.; Scientia Botanica. @AC 4529.

Both.; Ambo.

@AC 9166. "Both" (Exodus 22:11) = in each and all things, for in the inward sense "between both" does not mean between two, but in each and all things; for "two" = conjunction into one.

@9658. "Both" or "two" (Exodus 26:24) = conjunction.

Bottle.; Lagena.

@AC 2674. "(Hagar's) bottle of water" (Genesis 21:14) = very little truth. @2681. @2703.

@5567[2]. An earthen flask in his hand...

@AE 177[9]. "A bottle," or "potter's vessel" (Jeremiah 19:1) = falsity.

@374[13]. "A flagon" (Hosea 3:1) = that which contains, thus the ultimate sense of the Word, which they apply to their falsities and evils.

Bottle.; Uter.

@AR 672[2]. "Bottles," etc. = those things which are contained in them. Illustrated.

@839[2]. Bottles filled with iron filings... @TCR 116[end].

@TCR 38[2]. Like a bottle containing worms... @258.

@380[4]. Their mouth is like a bottle of honey, and their heart is like a bottle of gall.

@AE 195[15]. "Wine" = truth, and "bottles," the Knowledges which contain it.

@242[14]. "Earthen pitchers, the work of the hands of the potter" (Lamentations 4:2) = evils of life and falsities of doctrine which are from man's Own intelligence. (See also @177.)

@AE 376[28]. "Old bottles" (Matthew 9:17) = the statutes and judgments of the Jewish Church, and "new bottles," the Lord's injunctions and commands.

@--[34]. "Every bottle shall be filled with wine" (Jeremiah 13:12) = the mind of man, for this is a recipient of truth or falsity, as a bottle is of wine.

Bottomless pit. See <Deep-Abyssus>.

