@6833. "The bush burned with fire" = the perception that scientific truth was full of the good of Divine love.

@6834. "And the bush was not at all consumed" = Divine truth united to Divine good in the Natural.

@AE 295[10]. The "bush" in which the Lord appeared to Moses = this Divine love.

@403[16]. "Nor of a bramble bush do they gather grapes" (Luke 6:44). "Thorns" and "a bramble bush" = the evils which are opposite (to the good of the external and of the internal man).

Bramble.; Vepres. Vepretum.

