@654[13]. "They made her beautiful through the multitude of branches" (Ezekiel 31:9) = abundance of scientific truths rationally perceived.

@654[36]. All scientific and rational truths dissipated through evils and falsities is signified by "upon the mountains and in the valleys his branches are fallen" (Ezekiel 31:12).

Brass.; Aes.
Brazen.; Aeneus.
