@CL 77[end]. The twigs became shining brass with gold tips.

@AE 70. "Brass" = natural good, which is the ultimate good... The third age was called brazen or copper, because natural good then reigned, which is what is just and sincere of moral life.

@70[3]. "The shoe iron and brass" (Deuteronomy 33:25) = the lowest Natural from truth and good.

@176. Copper or brass = the good of the external or natural man.

@219[2]. "Walls of brass" (Jeremiah 1:18) = good protecting.

