Bucket.; Situla. Situlus.

@AC 3079[end]. "The waters shall pour out of the buckets" (Numbers 24:7) = truths from Knowledges.

@AE 406[end]. "A drop of a bucket" (Isaiah 40:15).

@Inv 17. They fall as into a bucket...

Buckler.; Scutum.
See <Shield>.

@AC 1231. Occurs. @AE 365[38].

@1788[4]. "Buckler and target" (Psalms 91:4) = protection against falsities.

@2832[2]. "Buckler," etc. (Psalms 18:2) are significative of the power of truth.

@9141[4]. "Buckler," "arrows" = truths of doctrine from the Word by means of which there is protection from the falsities of evil. References.

@AE 316[10]. "My buckler and the horn of my salvation" (Psalms 18:2) = salvation thence. "Buckler" is predicated of Divine good.

@357[31]. "Buckler" (Ezekiel 39:9) = falsity destroying good; "shield," falsity destroying truth.

@734[7]. "A buckler" (Psalms 35:2), because it defends the head, = protection against the falsities which destroy the understanding of truth; "a shield," because it defends the breast, = protection against the falsities which destroy charity, which is the will of good.

Bud. See <Germinate>.

Build.; Aedificare.

@AC 151. To "build" (Genesis 2:22) = to raise up -exstruere- what is fallen. @153.

@153. In the Word, to "build" is predicated of evils; to "erect," of falsities; and to "renew" of both. Illustrated.

@1187. "He built Nineveh" etc. (Genesis 10:11) = that thus he formed for himself doctrinal things of faith.

@1304. "Let us build us a city and a tower" (Genesis 11:4) = that they fashioned a doctrine and a worship. @1313.

@1324. "They ceased to build the city" (Genesis 11:8) = that such a doctrine was not received.

@1448. "He built an altar" = worship. @1618.

@1488. To collect scientifics and by their means rear up -exstruere- the external man, and build him, is not unlike building a house; wherefore "building" and "building houses" have a similar signification in the Word. Illustrated.

@1901. "Perchance I shall be built up by her" (Genesis 16:2) = that thus the Rational can be born...

@2601. They seem to themselves to be building small cities...

@2760. Preface [2]. "Rock" = this faith; upon this the Church is "built."

@2811. To "build an altar" (Genesis 22:9) = to prepare the Divine Human. Explained.

@3391[3]. To "build a house without righteousness, and chambers without judgment" (Jeremiah 22:13) = to put together what is religious from what is not good and not true.

@3916. "I shall also be built up by her" (Genesis 30:3) = that thus it will have life. To be "built up" = not to die, thus to rise again, or live.

@4390. "(Jacob) built himself a house" (Genesis 33:17) = the increase of good from truth in that state. To "build a house" = to instruct the external man in intelligence and wisdom; and as intelligence is of truth and wisdom of good, to "build a house," here = the increase of good from truth.

@4599[5]. To "build a tower" (Luke 14:28) = to procure for themselves interior truths.

@5117[7]. To "build the waste cities" (Amos 9:14) = to rectify the falsified doctrinal things of truth.

@6487. Illustrated by the building of houses... @TCR 152.

@9256[end]. "The builders" (Matthew 21:42) = those who are of the Church. @HH 534[end]. @AE 417[end].

@9857[5]. To "build chambers without judgment" = to imbue things which are not true.

@9954[13]. To "build Jerusalem" (Daniel 9:25) = to renew the Church. @AE 375[17]. @684[36].

@AR 153[8]. If they have been priests they want to build... But what they build by day falls down at night. @TCR 281[8].

@SE 3309. On those who desire to build.

@AE 355[9]. "Those afar off who will build in the temple of Jehovah" (Zechariah 6:15) = that those who formerly had been removed from the truths and goods of the Church will accede to the Church.

@391[17]. To "build the walls of Jerusalem" (Psalms 51:18) = to restore the Church by leading into the good of love, and teaching in the truths of doctrine.

@538[4]. The restoration of the Church and of doctrine is signified by "being inhabited," and "built" (Isaiah 44:26).

@617[12]. Under <House>, see this reference.

@706[18]. "He shall build my city" (Isaiah 45:13) = that he will restore the doctrine of truth.

@734[12]. Occurs. @811[19].

Build.; Condere.

@AC 2516[2]. From (the Rational) no doctrine of faith can begin, still less be built.

@10057[5]. By means of the Divine truth proceeding from the Lord's Divine good, Heaven is built and the Church is built.

@DLW 394. Building hypotheses.

@TCR 74[4]. From these he builds Heaven.

@95. On the building of the New Heaven. @108. @115. @118. @182.

@779. That a New Church will be built...

