@CL 269[2]. Occurs.

@SE 3358. (The Antediluvians) dwell deep under the buttocks.

Buttocks.; Nates.

@AC 818. Beneath the buttocks there is a horrible Hell... @SE 4505.

@5059. Under <Adultery>, see this reference, and at @5394. @SE 4563.

@5395[end]. They who have lived solely for themselves and for pleasure... are under the buttocks... @SE 4548.

@10409[6]. They who have come to honours and riches by machinations and cunning, there become magicians; they appear to sit beneath the buttocks...

@SE 3110. They who are under the buttocks answer to those who are in the zenith in a perpendicular line, because they are of such a nature; but those below at the buttocks are carried away by the cupidity of punishing everyone in a subtle manner... @4086.

@4049. On the cruel under the buttocks.

@4085. Such are in Hell under the buttocks, in most filthy excrements... @4461[end].

@4218. Under <Faith alone>, see this reference.

@AE 240[3]. "Their buttocks uncovered" (Isaiah 20:4) = the evils of self-love.

Buy.; Emere.
Buying. Purchase.; Emptio.
Buyer.; Emptor.

@AC 2048. "The purchase of money" (Genesis 17:12) = the spiritual. @2052. @2101. @2114.

@2937. To "buy," in the spiritual sense = to redeem. The spiritual are said to be "bought with silver," that is, to be redeemed with truth. @2964.

@2967[9]. "Buy without money" (Isaiah 55:1)... To "buy" = to procure for themselves.

@4106. "Purchase" (Genesis 31:18) = those things which have been acquired from another source.

@4397. To "buy" (Genesis 33:19) = to appropriate to himself.

@4487. "Acquisition," and "purchase" (Genesis 34:23) = truths... "Purchase," which is elsewhere called "the purchase of silver," = truth.

@4965. "Potiphar bought him"... To "buy" = that he ascribed these things to himself.

@5374. To "buy" (Genesis 41:57) = to procure for themselves, thus to appropriate. Spiritual procuring and appropriation are effected by means of good and truth; to this correspond the procuring and appropriation which are effected in the world by means of silver and gold... Hence "buying" = appropriation. Illustrated. @5406. @5410. @5426.

@5414. "The sons of Israel came to buy in the midst of those who came" (Genesis 42:5) = that he willed spiritual truths to be procured by means of scientifics equally as the rest... To "buy" = to procure.

@5433[3]. To "buy gold" (Revelation 3:18) = to procure and appropriate to themselves good. @AR 211. @AE 242.

@5435. "Thy servants are come to buy food" (Genesis 42:10) = that these truths are to be appropriated to the Natural by means of good... To "buy" = to be appropriated.

@5488. To buy with silver = to procure for one's self from what is one's own.

@5582. "Return ye, buy us a little food" (Genesis 43:2) = that in order for them to live, they should procure for themselves the good of spiritual truth. To "buy" = to procure and appropriate. @5588. @5655, @5820. @5886[4], Illustrated.

@5886. Under <Sell>, see this reference.

@6114. "For the provision which they bought" (Genesis 47:14) = that they should be supported by (the truth of the Church). To "buy" = to appropriate, and hence to be supported, because spiritual food is being treated of... which when appropriated, supports spiritual life.

@6137. "Buy us and our ground for bread" (Genesis 47:19) = the appropriation of both, in order that they may be supported with good. To "buy" = appropriation.

@6142. "Joseph bought the whole land of Egypt for Pharaoh" (Genesis 47:20) = that he appropriated to himself the whole natural mind where scientifics are, and placed it under the general auspices... in the Natural. @6153.

@6148. "Only the ground of the priests bought he not" (Genesis 47:22) = that the Internal from the Natural procured for itself the capacities of receiving good... "Not to buy" = not to appropriate to itself these capacities...

@6458. "Which Abraham bought" (Genesis 49:30) = redemption. To "buy" = to appropriate, thus also to redeem, for that which is redeemed is appropriated. @6461. @6549.

@7999. "The purchase of silver" (Exodus 12:44) = which has any spiritual truth. "Purchase" = acquisition and appropriation.

@8568[2]. To "buy wine and milk without price" = to procure for themselves the truth and good of faith from the Lord; thus gratis. @AE 376[4]. @617[10].

@8974. "When thou buyest a Hebrew servant" (Exodus 21:2)... To "buy" = to procure for one's self and appropriate. References.

@10109[4]. "They who are bought with silver" = those who have been converted.

@DSS 17[2]. To "buy" (Matthew 25) = to procure for themselves.

@AR 606. To "buy and sell" (Revelation 13:17) = to procure for themselves Knowledges... @606[end]. @AE 840.

@619. "Bought from the earth" (Revelation 14:3) = those who can be regenerated by the Lord, and thus redeemed in the world.

@SE 817[end]. (Spirits infusing a desire to buy certain things). @1333. @2169. @2954.

@AE 514[15]. "No buyer" (Deuteronomy 28:68) = that they are utterly vile.

@860. "Bought from the earth" = those who, having been instructed, received [truths] in the world. "The bought," or redeemed of the Lord, = those who receive instruction from the Word, especially concerning the Lord. @--[2], Explained.

@1139. "Not to buy any more" (Revelation 18:11) = to receive no more...

Buz.; Bus.

@AC 2864. "Buz," etc. = various religions and worships thence derived. @3240[4].

